.el .ds Aq '
.TH sentinel 1  "sentinel 0.2.0" 
.SH NAME
sentinel \- Scan Git repositories for secrets, vulnerable dependencies, and risky code patterns before commit or in CI
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsentinel\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan Git repositories for secrets, vulnerable dependencies, and risky code patterns before commit or in CI
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sentinel\-cache(1)
Inspect and empty the XDG advisory cache — the only state this tool keeps. Every destructive subcommand deletes only inside the resolved cache directory (resolved first, containment\-checked, then deleted), never follows symlinks out of it, and reports what it removed
.TP
sentinel\-completions(1)
Print the shell completion script for `<shell>` to stdout
.TP
sentinel\-scan(1)
Scan the Git repository at `[PATH]` for secrets (default: the cwd)
.TP
sentinel\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0
